# Commit message conventions

This repo does **not** ship commitlint or husky.
Still use Conventional Commits when the user asks you to commit.

```text
<type>(<scope>): <subject>
```

- Header ≤ 100 characters; no trailing period
- **type** lowercase: `feat` `fix` `perf` `refactor` `docs` `style` `test` `build` `ci` `chore` `revert`
- **scope** optional, lowercase, prefer a PLOS area: `domain` `engine` `ai` `storage` `stores` `features` `components` `i18n` `ui` `test` `docs` `tauri` `rust` `build` `chore`
- **subject** imperative or concise; the repo mixes English and 中文 subjects — match the surrounding history style
- Body/footer: wrap ≤ 100 characters; blank line before body
- Do not use `--no-verify` unless the user asks

```text
❌ BAD: Added assessment sync. | Feat: Fix UI
✅ GOOD: feat(ui): HomePage 今日启动器接入 activeGoal 上下文
✅ GOOD: fix(i18n): 对齐 zh/en 字典缺失键
✅ GOOD: test(engine): plan ETA 预估边界用例
```

Pass the message via HEREDOC so wrapping is preserved.
